      "content": "Privacy concerns are not just a debate but significant legal and ethical barriers that can legally stop the project if implemented without clear safeguards or if the government disregards public trust. While officials may emphasize efficiency, the risk of civil backlash and potential lawsuits often requires a much more nuanced \"social license\" than a simple budget approval. Ultimately, the decision usually hinges on whether the government can proactively address these valid ethical questions before moving forward.",
