    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like the \"ethical questions\" are always used as a way to stall tech that actually works. like, if we know for a fact it catches criminals and makes things run smoother, isn't it kind of irresponsible to let theoretical privacy worries block real-world safety improvements? isn't the \"nuance\" basically just an excuse for inaction?",
